ets near 99 percent, all in a state that has run well ahead of its nominal lean in federal races. Heavy outside spending against Stratton has not moved the polling, so the race stays rated Safe Democratic.", "watch": "A late shift among undecided voters toward Tracy, or a surge in outside spending, could narrow the margin, though the outcome would likely remain out of reach.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Dick Durbin (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "The open seat to succeed Dick Durbin strongly favors Democrat Juliana Stratton over Republican Don Tracy. Illinois has voted well left of its nominal partisan lean in recent federal races, and the 2026 environment adds to that edge. Both available polls show Stratton ahead by double digits, one by 13 points in early October and another by 17 in late October, and prediction markets put her chances at 98 to 99 percent. All eleven expert ratings place the race in the safest Democratic category.\n\nStratton has raised about $7.1 million to Tracy's $4.1 million, and outside groups have spent heavily on both sides, with slightly more opposing her than supporting her. That spending has not dented the polling picture. A minor independent candidate trails far behind. The seat is expected to remain comfortably in Democratic hands.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9877, "margin": 15.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9857, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9943, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9883, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9819, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9888, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9865, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9862, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9897, "margi